The function splits the text on newlines so each original line is wrapped independently. Within each line, it greedily adds words to the current output line while the total length stays within `width`, and starts a new line otherwise. A word longer than `width` is placed on its own line without being split. Blank lines are kept as empty lines. Runs of whitespace within a line are collapsed to single spaces, since `split()` treats them as word separators.

